- The shelf: ready made things to put on the canvas, one gesture each.
- A person opening the editor is offered objects they recognise — a calculator, a
- map, the two of them already wired, a plain block — and not the several hundred
- classes a pack declares. Those are still here, one level down, because laying
- out the inside of a page needs the primitives of mol and nothing else will do.
$bog_vmap_app_shelf $mol_view
	- The palette field, held by the editor and passed through: the shelf shows what
	- the scene has actually loaded, so there is one value and not two.
	links? \
	pack_link \
	land_classes /$mol_tree2
	- What the pointer is carrying, BY ITS ID, empty when nothing is being dragged,
	- and where the pointer is in viewport coordinates. The same protocol the
	- palette has always spoken, and now spoken in one place: a class row of the
	- second level writes its class name here through the binding below, a shelf row
	- writes the id of its item, and the id tells the two apart because a class name
	- starts with a dollar and an item id never does.
	dragged? \
	drag_x? 0
	drag_y? 0
	- Id of an item asked for by a plain click, which the editor answers by putting
	- it in the middle of the canvas. A press that turns into a drag never becomes a
	- click, so the two gestures do not fight.
	place? \
	classes_showed? false
	sub <= body /$mol_view
	-
	Title $mol_view
		sub /
			\Полка
	-
	Items $mol_list
		rows <= item_rows /
	-
	- The second level, folded away by default. A check and not an expander: the
	- palette has to GROW into whatever the shelf left, and inside an expander it
	- would sit in a list that sizes itself by its content, so the class list would
	- have no height to scroll in.
	Level $mol_check
		title \Все классы пака
		hint \Классы донорского пака целиком: примитивы, из которых верстают внутри блока
		checked? <=> classes_showed?
	-
	- The old palette, demoted to a second level. Rendered only while it is open,
	- so a folded panel does not fetch a pack tree it is not showing.
	Palette $bog_vmap_app_palette
		compact true
		links? <=> links?
		pack_link <= pack_link
		land_classes <= land_classes
		dragged? <=> dragged?
		drag_x? <=> drag_x?
		drag_y? <=> drag_y?
	-
	- One row per item. The same row the palette uses: a line of text that starts
	- carrying its item on `pointerdown`, because the native drag protocol cannot be
	- driven by synthetic events and would hand the drop to the browser.
	Item_row* $bog_vmap_app_palette_item
		title <= item_title* \
		hint <= item_hint* \
		click? <=> item_click*? null
		drag_start? <=> item_drag*? null
